 "c": [
  {"i":901,"t":["qualities","feelings"],"n":"意外 mainly describes events or results as unexpected (意外な結果, 意外に), so qualities comes first; the surprise feeling is secondary."},
  {"i":905,"t":["thinking","feelings"],"n":"The love sense (片思い, 思いを寄せる) is an emotion and fits feelings; a separate relationships entry is unnecessary."},
  {"i":935,"t":["function"],"s":{"4":["food"]},"n":"Learners meet it mainly in the grammar pattern 〜の代わりに; it does not describe things. The 'seconds/refill' sense (お代わり) belongs to food."},
  {"i":972,"t":["time"],"n":"Repetition and frequency are taught under time; the link to numbers is loose."},
  {"i":974,"t":["qualities"],"n":"A general descriptive adjective (有名な店, 有名な人); media is only a loose association."},
  {"i":990,"t":["communication"],"s":{"1":["transport"]},"n":"The core learner sense is being understood (言葉が通じる, 電話が通じる). The route sense is covered by the sense 1 transport entry, so movement is redundant."},
  {"i":1024,"t":["time","greetings"],"n":"Learners meet it mostly in the polite set phrase お待たせしました, which is a greetings item; relationships is loose."},
  {"i":1048,"t":["actions","media"],"n":"Typical uses are 鏡に映る and テレビに映る, or appearing in a photo: a general verb plus a screen or media sense. Arts is too loose."}
 ],
 "d": [
  {"i":903,"keep":[],"n":"'Imminent' extends the spatial sense; teach 目の前 under position."},
  {"i":918,"keep":[5],"n":"重い病気/けが is a core health collocation; 気が重い is idiomatic and fits feelings less well."},
  {"i":929,"keep":[],"n":"空気 as mood (空気を読む) is about the social atmosphere, not an emotion."},
  {"i":935,"keep":[],"n":"Learners meet 'seconds' as おかわり, a separate word; bare 代わり means substitute."},
  {"i":940,"keep":[5],"n":"計画を立てる / 目標を立てる is a very common N4 collocation for planning."},
  {"i":943,"keep":[4],"n":"機械を動かす (operate a machine) is common; 心を動かす is figurative."},
  {"i":948,"keep":[],"n":"期限が切れる is a state change and fits t; it is not a time-unit word."},
  {"i":955,"keep":[],"n":"Breaking up already fits relationships; divorce is 離婚 in the family unit."},
  {"i":960,"keep":[2],"n":"学校に通う / 会社に通う is the core usage and is taught in the school and work units."},
  {"i":961,"keep":[2,3],"n":"明るい色 belongs in the colours unit and 明るい性格 in character; both are very common."},
  {"i":976,"keep":[3],"n":"お茶 for tea ceremony (お茶を習う) is common and belongs in culture."},
  {"i":977,"keep":[],"n":"Learners meet 肉 as meat; flesh of the body is uncommon at this level (筋肉 is separate)."},
  {"i":989,"keep":[],"n":"人物 meaning someone's personality is less common; person/figure fits t."},
  {"i":990,"keep":[],"n":"道が駅に通じる is about a route leading somewhere, not a transport vocabulary item."},
  {"i":992,"keep":[3],"n":"注意する as warning or telling someone (先生に注意された) is common speech-act use."},
  {"i":995,"keep":[],"n":"黒い meaning suspicious or criminal is figurative slang."},
  {"i":1003,"keep":[],"n":"Time passing and 去る4月 are literary or formal; the core sense is leaving."},
  {"i":1012,"keep":[2],"n":"店が開く (shop opening hours) is taught in the shopping unit."},
  {"i":1032,"keep":[],"n":"経験を重ねる (repeat, accumulate) is abstract, not a time-unit word."},
  {"i":1039,"keep":[2],"n":"少々お待ちください (just a moment) is a very common set phrase for a short time."},
  {"i":1042,"keep":[5],"n":"パソコンが立ち上がる (boot up) is common everyday tech usage."}
